course: dictionary
lesson: 6746
title: Finding the right meaning in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one is meant. An onion is a round vegetable with layers and papery skin, and it is also the bulb of the plant it grows from. «Plants even fight back: an onion makes a stinging gas when you cut it» is about the vegetable, because you can cut it and it has a smell.
explain: Look for clues in the words near the word. «Onions, garlic, leeks and chives damage red blood cells in cats and dogs» tells you onions are food that can harm pets, even when they are cooked or powdered. The other words in the list show the sort of thing onion is.
explain: Then test your meaning. Put "a strong-smelling vegetable" into «The moonrat smells strongly of garlic or onion». It still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right. If it does not fit, look again at the clues.
fact: An onion is a round vegetable with layers, papery skin, and a strong smell and taste.
fact: The onion is a bulb: it stores food in its layers so the plant can grow again.
fact: Cutting an onion makes your eyes water, because it releases a gas that irritates your eyes.
fact: Spring onions are young onions, called scallions in the USA and Ireland.
fact: Onions are poisonous to dogs and cats, even when they are cooked or in powder form.
exercise: «The moonrat smells strongly of garlic or onion.» What kind of thing is an onion here? | A kind of drum | A colour of paint | *A strong-smelling vegetable | A soft white cloud
exercise: Why do your eyes water when you cut an onion? | You are sad when you cut food | Onions are full of tears | *It releases a gas that irritates your eyes | Knives make your eyes wet
exercise: Which of these is a young onion? | Onion powder | Red cabbage | *Spring onion | Onion soup
test: «Onions, garlic, leeks and chives damage red blood cells in cats and dogs.» What does this sentence warn you about? | Cats and dogs need onions every day | *Onions are dangerous for cats and dogs | Onions only grow in water | Onions are a good treat for pets
test: What does the bulb of an onion do? | *It stores food so the plant can grow again | It stops the plant from growing | It turns the onion into a gas | It makes the plant float on water
exam: «The moonrat smells strongly of garlic or onion.» Which clue helps you find the meaning of onion? | Smells strongly | It is not a rat | *Garlic, a food in the same list | The moonrat
